## SQ-RFX-07 | boot: Delight scripts bound to their pack, registrations through global.reg, no binding error
@group A
@commands Boot on the installed jars; read the KubeJS startup and server logs and latest.log
@pass `[creativedelight] core finished` in the startup log; the only `[reg] ... registered from the ... pack (override` line names `jrftl:prepared_flesh`; `[itemMerges] creativedelight: N merges` one more than the last run (the Engineer's Delight flour); no `forPack: invalid`, `ReferenceError`, `is not defined` or `Cannot find function` from a Delight script; latest.log has no mixin error naming `VintageLushGrassSeasonMixin` (it is gone) and `[salt] N Vintage salt blocks random tick` is present
@fails `[reg]` lines for creativedelight or creativeengineering ids: a registration id outside its pack (`namespace_lint.py -v`); `ReferenceError`: a dict alias swapped in a scope that does not bind it (`literal_id_swap.py` binds by file)
kjsexpect \[creativedelight\] core finished
kjsexpect \[itemMerges\] creativedelight: \d+ merges
kjsreject forPack: invalid|ReferenceError|is not defined|Cannot find function|registered from the creative(delight|engineering) pack
bootexpect \[salt\] \d+ Vintage salt blocks random tick
bootreject VintageLushGrassSeasonMixin
shell grep -hE '\[reg\] ' logs/kubejs/startup.log | sort -u | head -5
