@@section 6
@@title SQ-RFX Rules fixes P4 on an old-id save: More Mooblooms, Baby Mobs and Exposure Extras ids, 2026-11-17 ([plan_rules_fixes.md](../plan_rules_fixes.md) 14 and 12 V-06; TODO `conventions #30`, `conventions #23`)
@@date 2026-11-17
@@reviewed 2026-11-17
@@jars creativeworldgen creativecommon exposure
@@sources development/creativeWorldgen/members/mooblooms/src/main development/creativeWorldgen/members/babymobs/src/main/java development/creativeWorldgen/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/creativeworldgen/CreativeWorldgen.java development/exposureBackport/src/extras
@@text
@@text Mod ids `more_mooblooms` -> `moremooblooms` and `baby_mobs` -> `babymobs` (Worldgen members). Saves: `data/moremooblooms/swaps/owner_namespace.json` (namespace move plus aliases for the entity type and the spawn egg), saved `Variant` ids read through `MoobloomVariants.legacy`, member config files carried by Worldgen's `ConfigRename.carryOver`. Exposure Extras: the `creativeengineering:<tier>_camera_bag` ids are `replaces` entries now (the hand `MissingMappingsEvent` is gone). One old-id world: boot 1 writes it with the pre-rename Worldgen jar `jar_archive/p4_oldid/creativeworldgen-1.0.0.jar` (commit 5d1ed0a1; every other jar the installed one), boot 2 loads it after `tools/scratch_query/oldsave_swap.sh OUT` (the 2026-11-17 builds). The world must be fresh: a world opened once with the new jars and no swap list loses the old ids from level.dat ([forge-missing-mappings-staging](../agent_notes/forge-missing-mappings-staging.md)). SQ-BM-03 and SQ-EX-01 run in the same two boots.
@@table
## SQ-RFX-25 | old-id world: written with the pre-rename Worldgen, loaded with the new jars, no missing ids
@group A (old save, two boots)
@commands Boot 1: `NOSWAP=1` prep, replace `OUT/srv/mods/creativeworldgen-1.0.0.jar` with `jar_archive/p4_oldid/creativeworldgen-1.0.0.jar`, new superflat world; set `squidBabyChance = 0.75` in `config/baby_mobs-common.toml` and `regrowChance = 0.6` in `config/more_mooblooms-common.toml` (stop, edit, start); `> summon more_mooblooms:moobloom 0 -60 4 {NoAI:1b,Variant:"more_mooblooms:sunbloom",Tags:["p4a"]}`, the same with `more_mooblooms:rosebloom` at 0 -60 6 and an `Age:-24000` calf of `more_mooblooms:lilybloom` at 0 -60 8; `> setblock 0 -61 10 chest{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"more_mooblooms:moobloom_spawn_egg",Count:3b,tag:{EntityTag:{Variant:"more_mooblooms:peonybloom"}}}]}`; `> summon squid 0 -59 12 {Age:-24000,NoAI:1b}` in a water pool; `> save-all`; stop. Run `oldsave_swap.sh OUT`; boot 2 on the SAME world; grep latest.log
@pass boot 2 log: `[swaps] ... namespace move(s)` counts the list, `[swaps] minecraft:entity_type: 1 id(s) remapped` and the same for `minecraft:item`; `[swaps] config more_mooblooms-common.toml carried over to moremooblooms-common.toml` and the `baby_mobs` one; no `Identifier .* is missing` / missing registry entry naming `more_mooblooms` or `baby_mobs`; `config/` holds `moremooblooms-common.toml` (`regrowChance = 0.6`) and `babymobs-common.toml` (`squidBabyChance = 0.75`), the old files gone
@fails ids missing: the swap list is not in the moreMooblooms member jar (`data/moremooblooms/swaps/`) or the world was opened once without it; a config at defaults: `CreativeWorldgen` did not call `carryOver` before Forge read the COMMON configs
@draft boot 1 needs the archived jar swapped into OUT/srv/mods and a stop, config edit and restart in the middle; qrun has no step for a jar swap inside one row. Boot 2 checks below are runnable once the world exists
shell ! grep -E "Identifier .* is missing|[Mm]issing.*(more_mooblooms|baby_mobs):" logs/latest.log
shell grep -hE "\[swaps\]" logs/latest.log | head -12
shell grep -n "regrowChance\|squidBabyChance" config/moremooblooms-common.toml config/babymobs-common.toml; ls config | grep -E "mooblooms|baby_?mobs"
## SQ-RFX-26 | old-id world: mooblooms keep their variants, eggs keep theirs
@group A (old save, boot 2 of SQ-RFX-25)
@commands `/cdevtest entities 0 -60 6 8 type=moremooblooms:moobloom`; `> data get entity @e[type=moremooblooms:moobloom,tag=p4a,limit=1,sort=nearest] Variant` for each; `> data get block 0 -61 10 Items`; take one egg and use it on the ground at 4 -60 4; `> data get entity @e[type=moremooblooms:moobloom,limit=1,sort=nearest,x=4,y=-60,z=4] Variant`
@pass three mooblooms load as `moremooblooms:moobloom` with `Variant: "moremooblooms:sunbloom"`, `"moremooblooms:rosebloom"`, `"moremooblooms:lilybloom"` (the calf still a calf), no `unknown variant` WARN; the chest holds 3 `moremooblooms:moobloom_spawn_egg`; the egg spawns a peonybloom
@fails a moobloom gone: the entity type was not remapped (SQ-RFX-25); a plain `moremooblooms:moobloom` variant with an `unknown variant` WARN: `MoobloomVariants.legacy` not applied in `Moobloom.readAdditionalSaveData`; an egg giving a random variant: `MoobloomSpawnEggItem.variantOf`
> cdevtest entities 0 -60 6 8 type=moremooblooms:moobloom
> data get block 0 -61 10 Items
expect moremooblooms:moobloom_spawn_egg
shell ! grep -E "has unknown variant 'more_mooblooms:" logs/latest.log
look each moobloom's Variant reads the moremooblooms: id it was summoned with; the egg used on the ground gives a peonybloom
## SQ-RFX-27 | old ids in NBT on a fresh world resolve through the aliases (mooblooms, camera bags)
@group A
@commands Fresh world, new jars: `> setblock 20 -61 0 chest{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"more_mooblooms:moobloom_spawn_egg",Count:1b},{Slot:1b,id:"creativeengineering:leather_camera_bag",Count:1b},{Slot:2b,id:"creativeengineering:iron_camera_bag",Count:1b},{Slot:3b,id:"creativeengineering:netherite_camera_bag",Count:1b},{Slot:4b,id:"exposure_extras:camera_bag",Count:1b}]}`; `> data get block 20 -61 0 Items`; `> setblock 22 -61 0 spawner{SpawnData:{entity:{id:"more_mooblooms:moobloom"}}}`; `> data get block 22 -61 0 SpawnData`
@pass the chest lists `moremooblooms:moobloom_spawn_egg`, `exposureextras:leather_camera_bag`, `exposureextras:iron_camera_bag`, `exposureextras:netherite_camera_bag`, `exposureextras:camera_bag` (5 stacks, none `minecraft:air`); the spawner keeps a moobloom; boot log: `[swaps] N permanent alias(es) in the active registries` (N counts these 6 ids among the rest)
@fails a camera bag gone: the `creativeengineering:` ids are not `replaces` entries in Exposure's `owner_namespace.json` (V-06); the egg gone: the moremooblooms `replaces` entry
> setblock 20 -61 0 chest{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"more_mooblooms:moobloom_spawn_egg",Count:1b},{Slot:1b,id:"creativeengineering:leather_camera_bag",Count:1b},{Slot:2b,id:"creativeengineering:iron_camera_bag",Count:1b},{Slot:3b,id:"creativeengineering:netherite_camera_bag",Count:1b},{Slot:4b,id:"exposure_extras:camera_bag",Count:1b}]}
> data get block 20 -61 0 Items
expect moremooblooms:moobloom_spawn_egg
expect exposureextras:leather_camera_bag
expect exposureextras:iron_camera_bag
expect exposureextras:netherite_camera_bag
expect exposureextras:camera_bag
> setblock 22 -61 0 spawner{SpawnData:{entity:{id:"more_mooblooms:moobloom"}}}
> data get block 22 -61 0 SpawnData
expect moremooblooms:moobloom
reject (Unknown (item|block|block type|entity)|Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command)

