@@sources development/creativeWorldgen/members/mooblooms/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/moremooblooms/MoreMooblooms.java development/creativeWorldgen/members/mooblooms/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/moremooblooms/compat/BuzzierBeesSet.java development/creativeWorldgen/members/mooblooms/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/moremooblooms/MMConfig.java
@@text
@@text The `blueprint` content set and the Buzzier Bees sub-packs `replace_two_by_two` and `remove_sunny_from_all_effects` were deleted with their switches. The other Buzzier Bees sub-packs and the tag-compat packs still load.
@@table
## SQ-RFX-29 | More Mooblooms adds no advancement modifier packs; the other Buzzier Bees sub-packs still load
@group A (the pack's mods, Buzzier Bees and Blueprint present)
@commands Boot to the world; `/datapack list`; `shell` checks of the log and `config/moremooblooms-common.toml`
@pass `/datapack list` shows no `moremooblooms:blueprint`, `moremooblooms:buzzier_bees/replace_two_by_two` or `moremooblooms:buzzier_bees/remove_sunny_from_all_effects`, and still shows `moremooblooms:buzzier_bees/disable_moobloom_spawns` and `moremooblooms:alexsmobs`; the config file has no `replaceTwoByTwo` or `removeSunnyFromAllEffects` key; no ERROR from moremooblooms
@fails a deleted pack still listed: the jar in mods/ predates the change; a missing sub-pack: `BuzzierBeesSet.dataSwitches` lost more than the two entries
> datapack list
shell ! grep -nE "replaceTwoByTwo|removeSunnyFromAllEffects" config/moremooblooms-common.toml
shell ! grep -nE "ERROR.*moremooblooms" logs/latest.log
look `/datapack list` output: the three packs absent, `buzzier_bees/disable_moobloom_spawns` and `alexsmobs` present

@@section 10
@@title SQ-RFX Follow-up F5 and F7: the flower tags' item side in Creative Compat, the loot tags in Creative Loot, 2026-11-17 ([plan_rules_fixes_followup.md](../plan_rules_fixes_followup.md); [creative_compat.md](../creative_compat.md) 5; [breeding_audit.md](../breeding_audit.md))
@@date 2026-11-17
@@reviewed 2026-11-17
@@jars creativecompat creativecommon creativeloot
@@sources kubejs/data/creativecompat/kubejs/tags/flower_tags.js kubejs/server_scripts/tags/animal_tags.js kubejs/data/creativeloot/kubejs/tags/loottags.js
@@text
@@text The removal of wild plants, Botania special flowers, the flower crown and the azalea piles from the flower item tags moved into Creative Compat's `flower_tags.js` with the floating, planter box and flower box tags that keep them (same content, order now inside one file). The loot group tags are `#creativeloot:loot/*` (checked: no reader of `creativeworldgen:loot/` is left).
@@table
## SQ-RFX-30 | tags: floats, planter box, flower box, flower and loot tags equal the baseline after the move
@group A
@commands `/dumpall`; `python3 $INST/tools/dump_diff.py tags $INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_rules_p3a_2026-11-17 kubejs/exported --rename creativeworldgen:loot/=creativeloot:loot/` (or against the dump of the commit c65c5871 jars)
@pass `TAGS_SAME` for `creativecompat:physics/floats`, `creativecompat:flower_box_plants`, `another_furniture:planter_box_placeables`, `minecraft:flowers`, `minecraft:small_flowers`, `minecraft:tall_flowers`, `creativeloot:loot/chalk` and `creativeloot:loot/golden_food`; any other tag line is explained in the run doc
@fails a flower tag still holding a `wild_` item or a Botania special flower: Compat's `flower_tags.js` ran before a script that fills the flower tags (load order between script packs), or the jar is not installed; floats missing the wild plants: the same order problem, or `t.add` ran after the removal
shell python3 "$INST/tools/dump_diff.py" tags "$INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_rules_p3a_2026-11-17" kubejs/exported --rename creativeworldgen:loot/=creativeloot:loot/ | grep -E "physics/floats|flower_box_plants|planter_box_placeables|minecraft:(small_|tall_)?flowers|loot/(chalk|golden_food)|TAGS_SAME" | tail -20
look the grep output: no ONLY_ or changed line for the eight tags
## SQ-RFX-31 | float tag members: the wild plants and Botania special flowers float, bees and hummingbirds lose them
@group A
@commands `/cdevtest tag item creativecompat:physics/floats`, `/cdevtest tag item minecraft:flowers`
@pass the floats tag lists wild plants (for example `wild_onions` ids of the Delight crops), `botania` special flower ids (with Botania), `immersive_weathering:flower_crown` and the azalea leaf and flower piles; `minecraft:flowers` lists none of the `wild_` items, no Botania special flower, no flower crown
@fails floats without the wild plants: `flower_tags.js` did not run or read the flower tag after the removal; flowers still holding wild plants: the removal did not run (script error in the log, search `flower_tags`)
> cdevtest tag item creativecompat:physics/floats
> cdevtest tag item minecraft:flowers
waitlog verb=tag kind=item tag=creativecompat:physics/floats n= [1-9]\d*
reject verb=tag kind=item tag=minecraft:flowers n=\d+ ids=.*:wild_
shell ! grep -nE "(ERROR|Error).*flower_tags" logs/kubejs/server.log
look the floats tag member list (wild plants, special flowers, crown, piles) and the flowers list without them
## SQ-RFX-32 | loot tag probe: the chalk tag holds the chalks and the box, under creativeloot
@group A
@commands `/cdevtest tag item creativeloot:loot/chalk`, `/cdevtest tag item creativeloot:loot/golden_food`, `/cdevtest tag item creativeworldgen:loot/chalk`
@pass the chalk tag lists every chalk stick and the chalk box, the golden food tag lists the golden apple, golden carrot and Golden Food's plain golden foods; the `creativeworldgen:loot/chalk` probe shows an empty or missing tag
@fails `creativeloot:loot/chalk` empty: `tags/loottags.js` did not load (Creative Loot not installed); the worldgen id filled: a script still names it
> cdevtest tag item creativeloot:loot/chalk
> cdevtest tag item creativeloot:loot/golden_food
> cdevtest tag item creativeworldgen:loot/chalk
waitlog verb=tag kind=item tag=creativeloot:loot/chalk n= [1-9]\d*
reject verb=tag kind=item tag=creativeworldgen:loot/chalk n= [1-9]\d*
look the two creativeloot lists are full and the worldgen id has no members
